DB2 me check karne ke liye ki kisi table me LOB columns (BLOB, CLOB, DBCLOB) hain ya nahi, ye query chalao:

SELECT COLNAME,
       TYPENAME,
       LENGTH
FROM SYSCAT.COLUMNS
WHERE TABSCHEMA = 'DEV_BIP_T'
  AND TABNAME   = 'CSS_ROLE_LOCALES'
  AND TYPENAME IN ('BLOB','CLOB','DBCLOB');

Agar rows return hoti hain Jaise:

COLNAME        TYPENAME
-------------  --------
DOCUMENT       CLOB
IMAGE_DATA     BLOB

To table me LOB columns hain.

Agar koi row return nahi hoti
To table me LOB columns nahi hain.
Table ke saare columns dekhne ke liye

SELECT COLNAME,
       TYPENAME,
       LENGTH
FROM SYSCAT.COLUMNS
WHERE TABSCHEMA = 'DEV_BIP_T'
  AND TABNAME   = 'CSS_ROLE_LOCALES';

Pure schema me kaunsi tables LOB use karti hain:

SELECT DISTINCT TABSCHEMA,
                TABNAME
FROM SYSCAT.COLUMNS
WHERE TABSCHEMA = 'DEV_BIP_T'
  AND TYPENAME IN ('BLOB','CLOB','DBCLOB')
ORDER BY TABNAME;


Agar sirf quickly check karna hai to:

SELECT COUNT(*)
FROM SYSCAT.COLUMNS
WHERE TABSCHEMA='DEV_BIP_T'
  AND TABNAME='CSS_ROLE_LOCALES'
  AND TYPENAME IN ('BLOB','CLOB','DBCLOB');

Result 0 aaye to LOB nahi hai, 0 se bada aaye to LOB column present hai.
